<title>ITALY: Italy 1997 new car market seen over 2 mln - Anfia.</title>
<headline>Italy 1997 new car market seen over 2 mln - Anfia.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's new car market is forecast to top two million units in 1997 after the good progress seen in the first four months of the year, Italy's vehicle manufacturing association Anfia said.</p>
<p>Earlier, Italy's Ministry of Transport said new car registrations were up 52.37 percent in April 1997 to 231,500, compared to April 1996, and this month was the best month in the Italian new car market since July 1992 when registrations reached 234,931 units.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
